# PLAYER CANNOT MOVE WHEN THIS DIALOGUE TIMELINE STARES
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": "Is this thing on...?"
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": "Ahem..."
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": "Hello, hello! You’re probably wondering why you’re here."
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": “Well… you died! HAHAHA!”
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": “Fortunately - or unfortunately, depending on how you look at it - for you, the afterlife is currently full. So, I’ve put together a little game for the wandering souls out there, and it happens to be your turn.”
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": “Get through my house of puzzles and you can have your life back!”
# dialogue pauses in code until player moves around a bit first
set {playerMove} = true
[wait time="3.5"]
set {playerMove} = false
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": “What’s that? You’re stuck? …Think again!”
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": “You currently exist in a half-state somewhere between the mortal and spiritual planes. With this state comes the unique ability to shift between a bodily and ghostly form."
"MYSTERIOUS VOICE": "Try it now by pressing the Z key and those pesky bars will pesk you no more!”
set {playerMove} = true